    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463-a1">

                <pb facs="0458" n="360" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg360"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram from Marquis Venosta to Baron
                        Fava.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Italian Embassy</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic">October 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Copy left with Mr. Adee by Baron Fava.)</p>
                <p>The minister of the King at Pekin communicates the response made by the
                    diplomatic corps to the three points of the German circular: <pb facs="0459"
                        n="361" xml:id="pg361"/>
                    <list>
                        <item>First. Other culprits besides those designated ought to be
                            punished.</item>
                        <item>Second. The indicated penalties are insufficient.</item>
                        <item>Third. The presence of delegates of the legations could alone assure
                            the execution.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Be pleased to telegraph the views of the Secretary of State.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Visconti-Venosta.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
